# Field Lessons — Living Memory

> One lesson per defect that was actually met in production. A lesson without
> a reproducible incident is an opinion; keep opinions out of this log.
> Format: date · incident (root cause) · the rule it produced · how to detect it early.

---

## Template entry (copy, fill, delete nothing silently)

### [YYYY-MM-DD] — Short incident name
- **Symptom:** what was observed (the false green, the invisible feature, the wrong number…)
- **Root cause:** what actually happened beneath the symptom.
- **Reconciliation trap:** why the wrong answer still "made sense" on the surface.
- **Rule produced:** the protocol/rule now encoded in the playbook (P#, §#).
- **Early detection:** the check that would have caught it in minutes, not hours.

---

## Example (shape only — replace with your own incidents)

### [2026-01-15] — Stale container serving pre-change binaries
- **Symptom:** verified code change, green suite, yet the endpoint served the old behavior for hours.
- **Root cause:** the serving container was started before the change; a rebuild without restart is not a deploy.
- **Reconciliation trap:** the code was provably correct, so everyone trusted the runtime instead of reading it.
- **Rule produced:** P2.5 — read `docker ps` + `docker inspect` (started-at vs change-time) before any visibility claim.
- **Early detection:** `check-env.ps1` at session start; any container older than the newest binary is a stop.
